The changed code removes the `ORDER_PATTERN` regex gate and instead validates ordering strings by resolving them through `names_to_path()`, which raises `FieldError` for any name that does not resolve to a real field/annotation. This is a strict allowlist-style validation (only resolvable model fields pass), and the ordering values are still passed to the ORM as field names (bound/resolved), not concatenated into raw SQL. The admin path derives `order_field` from `list_display`/`admin_order_field` (developer-controlled), and the public `order_by()` path now rejects unresolvable names. No attacker-influenced value reaches SQL text unbound or unallowlisted.

